{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem.\n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born in 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was the sister of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem and Queen Melisende of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152 when he was only 12 years old. His mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age.\n\nRaymond III was a member of the House of Toulouse and the last count of the Crusader state of Tripoli. He played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the County of Tripoli during the 12th century.\n\n*Marriage and Alliances*\nIn 1164 Raymond III married Eschiva of Bures the widow of Walter of Saint-Omer. The marriage was likely a strategic alliance to strengthen his position in the region. Raymond III also formed alliances with the Byzantine Empire and the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin and Its Aftermath*\nIn 1187 Raymond III was defeated by Saladin at the Battle of Hattin. The battle was a significant defeat for the Crusader states and led to the loss of Jerusalem and other territories. Raymond III was captured by Saladin but was later released. He died in 1187 possibly due to injuries sustained during the battle.\n\nRaymond III's death marked the end of the House of Toulouse's rule in Tripoli. The county was later inherited by Bohemond IV of Antioch who established the House of Poitou's rule in Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35264554619789124}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.81470454158261